2025-05-01 01:49:34 - Thread-489 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant columns and their potential usage (only the tables listed in the catalogue are mentioned)

ORDERS  
• "order_id": primary key for order‐level joins  
• "user_id": link to USERS."id"  
• "created_at": micro‑second epoch time when the order was placed – filter for 2021 ( >= 1609459200000000 AND < 1640995200000000 )  
• "status": can be used to keep / remove “Cancelled” orders if required  
• "num_of_item": sanity‑check (not really needed for the requested KPIs)

USERS  
• "id": primary key – joins to ORDERS / ORDER_ITEMS  
• "created_at": registration date – keep only users who registered in 2021 (same micro‑second boundaries)  
• "country": required in the GROUP BY clause  
• (other demographics: "gender", "state", …) – not needed here

ORDER_ITEMS  
• "order_id": link to ORDERS."order_id"  
• "inventory_item_id": link to INVENTORY_ITEMS."id"  
• "user_id": redundant copy of USERS."id" (can be helpful)  
• "product_id": link to PRODUCTS if needed  
• "sale_price": not used for profit (we have to use retail minus cost)

INVENTORY_ITEMS  
• "id": primary key – join to ORDER_ITEMS  
• "created_at": creation date – keep items created in 2021  
• "cost": unit cost (needed for profit)  
• "product_retail_price": unit retail price (needed for profit)  
• "product_department": required in the GROUP BY clause  
• "product_category": required in the GROUP BY clause

PRODUCTS (optional)  
• "id": sometimes used instead of INVENTORY_ITEMS’ shadow columns; not strictly required because INVENTORY_ITEMS already carries department & category as denormalised fields.

Typical filter conditions  
• ORDERS."created_at"   BETWEEN 1609459200000000 AND 1640995200000000  
• USERS."created_at"     BETWEEN 1609459200000000 AND 1640995200000000  
• INVENTORY_ITEMS."created_at" BETWEEN 1609459200000000 AND 1640995200000000  



Exploratory Snowflake queries (each capped with LIMIT 20)

```sql
--Description: 1. Sample users who registered in 2021 (country snapshot).
SELECT
    "id",
    "country",
    "created_at"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."USERS"
WHERE "created_at" >= 1609459200000000
  AND "created_at" <  1640995200000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2. Sample orders placed in 2021.
SELECT
    "order_id",
    "user_id",
    "created_at",
    "status"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDERS"
WHERE "created_at" >= 1609459200000000
  AND "created_at" <  1640995200000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3. Join orders (2021) with their purchasers who also registered in 2021.
SELECT
    o."order_id",
    o."created_at"            AS "order_ts",
    u."created_at"            AS "user_reg_ts",
    u."country"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDERS"  o
JOIN "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."USERS"   u
  ON o."user_id" = u."id"
WHERE o."created_at" BETWEEN 1609459200000000 AND 1640995200000000
  AND u."created_at" BETWEEN 1609459200000000 AND 1640995200000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4. Observe inventory items that were created in 2021.
SELECT
    "id",
    "product_id",
    "product_department",
    "product_category",
    "cost",
    "product_retail_price",
    "created_at"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."INVENTORY_ITEMS"
WHERE "created_at" >= 1609459200000000
  AND "created_at" <  1640995200000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5. Orders (2021), their items, and inventory lines created in 2021 (raw join, one record per item).
SELECT
    oi."order_id",
    oi."inventory_item_id",
    inv."product_department",
    inv."product_category",
    inv."cost",
    inv."product_retail_price"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"      oi
JOIN "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDERS"           o   ON oi."order_id" = o."order_id"
JOIN "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."INVENTORY_ITEMS"  inv ON oi."inventory_item_id" = inv."id"
WHERE o."created_at"  BETWEEN 1609459200000000 AND 1640995200000000
  AND inv."created_at" BETWEEN 1609459200000000 AND 1640995200000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6. Add user dimension to previous join (country in view).
SELECT
    u."country",
    oi."order_id",
    inv."product_department",
    inv."product_category",
    inv."product_retail_price",
    inv."cost"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDERS"           o
JOIN "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."USERS"            u   ON o."user_id" = u."id"
JOIN "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"      oi  ON oi."order_id" = o."order_id"
JOIN "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."INVENTORY_ITEMS"  inv ON inv."id"     = oi."inventory_item_id"
WHERE o."created_at"  BETWEEN 1609459200000000 AND 1640995200000000
  AND u."created_at"  BETWEEN 1609459200000000 AND 1640995200000000
  AND inv."created_at" BETWEEN 1609459200000000 AND 1640995200000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7. Compute profit per order (still limited to 2021 filters).
SELECT
    oi."order_id",
    SUM(inv."product_retail_price" - inv."cost") AS "order_profit"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"      oi
JOIN "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDERS"           o   ON oi."order_id" = o."order_id"
JOIN "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."INVENTORY_ITEMS"  inv ON inv."id"     = oi."inventory_item_id"
WHERE o."created_at"  BETWEEN 1609459200000000 AND 1640995200000000
  AND inv."created_at" BETWEEN 1609459200000000 AND 1640995200000000
GROUP BY oi."order_id"
ORDER BY oi."order_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8. Distinct countries represented in 2021 qualified orders.
SELECT DISTINCT
    u."country"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDERS"  o
JOIN "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."USERS"   u
  ON o."user_id" = u."id"
WHERE o."created_at" BETWEEN 1609459200000000 AND 1640995200000000
  AND u."created_at" BETWEEN 1609459200000000 AND 1640995200000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9. Monthly order counts (by numeric month extracted via date_tz trick; here we avoid conversion and use TO_TIMESTAMP).
SELECT
    DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP(o."created_at" / 1000000)) AS "order_month",
    COUNT(DISTINCT o."order_id")                               AS "orders_in_month"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDERS" o
WHERE o."created_at" BETWEEN 1609459200000000 AND 1640995200000000
GROUP BY 1
ORDER BY 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10. Final‑shaped aggregate (month, country, department, category) – preview only, 20 rows max.
SELECT
    DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP(o."created_at" / 1000000))               AS "order_month",
    u."country",
    inv."product_department",
    inv."product_category",
    COUNT(DISTINCT o."order_id")                                              AS "num_orders",
    COUNT(DISTINCT o."user_id")                                               AS "unique_purchasers",
    SUM(inv."product_retail_price" - inv."cost")                              AS "profit"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDERS"           o
JOIN "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."USERS"            u   ON o."user_id"           = u."id"
JOIN "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"      oi  ON oi."order_id"         = o."order_id"
JOIN "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."INVENTORY_ITEMS"  inv ON inv."id"              = oi."inventory_item_id"
WHERE o."created_at"  BETWEEN 1609459200000000 AND 1640995200000000
  AND u."created_at"  BETWEEN 1609459200000000 AND 1640995200000000
  AND inv."created_at" BETWEEN 1609459200000000 AND 1640995200000000
GROUP BY
    DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP(o."created_at" / 1000000)),
    u."country",
    inv."product_department",
    inv."product_category"
ORDER BY "order_month", "country", "product_department", "product_category"
LIMIT 20;
```

These ten queries progress from simple inspections of individual tables to a fully joined, grouped preview of the desired metrics while strictly following the scope and quoting conventions requested.
